<main class="container academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/blog'>Learning library</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">lesson <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1>Deploying and Maintaining a Static Website</h1><p>A reliable deployment process makes the published output predictable and gives you a way to detect regressions before and after release.</p></section><div class="academy-reading-layout"><aside class="academy-toc"><p class="academy-kicker">IN THIS GUIDE</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#section-1"><span>01</span>Confirm the publish directory</a><a href="#section-2"><span>02</span>Keep redirects direct</a><a href="#section-3"><span>03</span>Set sensible response headers</a><a href="#section-4"><span>04</span>Use a repeatable test checklist</a><a href="#section-5"><span>05</span>Deploy with a rollback path</a></nav><div class="academy-author"><img src="/assets/images/mbk-personal-favicon-96.png" width="38" height="38" alt=""><div>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Founder, MBK Global</small></div></div><p class="academy-read-note">2 min read · Practical learning notes<br>Learn. Apply. Make it your own.</p><a class='academy-text-link' href='/resources'>More learning resources ↗</a></aside><div class="academy-reading-body"><article class="content-page"><header><p class="eyebrow">MBK Global · Practical guide</p></header><section><h2 id="section-1">Confirm the publish directory</h2><p>Identify which directory the host actually publishes and keep hosting configuration files such as Netlify _headers and _redirects in the appropriate publish root. Do not assume a configuration file for another provider controls the live deployment.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-2">Keep redirects direct</h2><p>Use permanent redirects only when a URL has a close, useful replacement. Avoid loops, chains and redirecting unrelated pages to the homepage. Update internal links and sitemap entries to point directly to final canonical URLs.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-3">Set sensible response headers</h2><p>Use HTTPS, nosniff, a restrictive referrer policy and framing protection appropriate to the site. Begin Content Security Policy in report-only mode when existing inline code or third-party resources may be affected. Review reports before enforcement.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-4">Use a repeatable test checklist</h2><p>Check HTML structure, internal links, metadata, canonical URLs, sitemap coverage, structured data, image references, keyboard navigation and responsive layouts. Record the command and result for each test rather than marking unrun checks as passed.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-5">Deploy with a rollback path</h2><p>Keep an untouched source backup and a separate implementation copy. Review the diff, publish only after owner review, then test live status codes, redirects and headers. Keep Search Console and real-user performance monitoring as post-deployment tasks.</p></section>
<p><strong>About this guide:</strong> This is general educational guidance. Adapt recommendations to your site's actual stack, risk and audience, and verify changes before publishing.</p>
<p>Explore related work: <a href='/web-development'>web development</a>, <a href='/projects'>projects</a>, and <a href='/contact'>contact</a>.</p></article></div></div><div data-portrait-track data-caption="The person behind the work"></div></main>
